        "title": "fix(repair): close staged proof review gaps",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nThis draft hardens ClawSweeper's staged proof and comment-router paths while keeping mutation safety fail-closed.\n\nThe latest repair pass rebases the full stack onto `e8a48a1b5116c9017ddd065a202ca46c9466eeea` and fixes the three fresh P1s:\n\n1. autoclose and maintainer-engagement safety use complete, separately refreshed comment hydration; bounded newest-tail discovery is routing-only\n2. forced replay uses durable distinct attempt identities, survives terminal history, and completes every coalesced pending attempt\n3. broad discovery pages distinct item identities before bounded per-item hydration, so one hot item's comments cannot starve older items\n\nIt also closes the narrow exact-range review findings around REST tail pagination, per-item candidate reservation, claimed-stage preservation, and proof-input capacity. The proof ceiling is now 250,000 entries, above the observed supported OpenClaw checkout.\n\n## Latest repair commits\n\n- `d38effea4f` `fix(router): isolate autoclose safety hydration`\n- `e26d85de6e` `fix(router): preserve forced replay attempts`\n- `1975a19d5e` `fix(router): page broad scans by item`\n- `6b05b20e4e` `fix(router): preserve bounded discovery progress`\n- `6821bb4151` `fix(repair): raise staged proof entry ceiling`\n\n## Validation\n\n- exact head: `6821bb415117b23978be484edc41f9dd3df87379`\n- exact tree: `1ada3d7ba08dcd5b608e0f1b1fdc4d9327d1edc7`\n- rebased base: `e8a48a1b5116c9017ddd065a202ca46c9466eeea`\n- Node: `v26.5.0`\n- focused router, pagination, target-validation, strict-binding, and workflow suite: `383/383`\n- full `pnpm --config.verify-deps-before-run=false run check`: passed on the exact tree\n  - unit: `1088` passed, `2` skipped, `0` failed\n  - repair: `945/945`\n  - changed coverage: `100.00%` lines, `86.90%` branches, `100.00%` functions\n  - aggregate coverage: `74.54%` lines, `73.73%` branches, `84.65%` functions\n  - builds, lint, active-surface/limit checks, and formatting over `362` files passed\n- `git diff --check`: passed\n\n## Draft blocker\n\nThe exact-item fanout still relies on a shared GitHub Actions concurrency group. GitHub retains only one pending run per concurrency group, so a burst can replace an older pending dispatcher rather than behaving as a durable queue. The PR remains draft and unmerged pending a queue-safe dispatcher design.\n",
